            "reviewer": {
                "name": "garybeihl",
                "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                "username": "garybeihl"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\nFair question - I overclaimed. In upstream, add() only updates responderInfos, and the only consumer is run() at startup. There is no eager-attestation hook on add() in upstream; the language I used describes behavior that exists only on the integration branch (where notifyDeviceAdded triggers SPDMResponderManager to re-attest).\n\nFor upstream, the honest framing is: this is a behavior-correctness building block - establishing last-write-wins semantics for add() so that when the runtime re-discovery code lands (D-Bus InterfacesAdded re-firing for the same path on device reset/firmware update), the dedup decision is already correct in the canonical place. Without this, runtime re-discovery would either need its own special-case (early-return loses fresh state) or have to add explicit erase-before-add logic at every callsite.\n\nReworded PS2 along those lines. Let me know if you would prefer to defer this change until the runtime re-discovery code that needs it is also in review."
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1780345205,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Patrick Williams",
                "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                "username": "williamspatrick"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n(1 comment)"
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1780345726,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "garybeihl",
                "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                "username": "garybeihl"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\nMakes sense - I'll park this one and refresh it when the runtime re-discovery code is up for review. The dedup choice will read more cleanly next to the D-Bus object lifecycle changes anyway."
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1782904657,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "garybeihl",
                "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                "username": "garybeihl"
            },
            "message": "Abandoned\n\nAbandoning \u2014 this delete-recreate approach to SPDMDiscovery::add() dedup is superseded by the same-path guard in 90799 (now merged), which handles the duplicate-add case more simply. No longer needed."
        }
    ],
